    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fixes are ready. To summarize:\n\n**The issue:** When parsing `39.95`, JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic produces `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995` when multiplying by 100 to convert to cents. This failed the integer validation in `store.js`.\n\n**The fix:** I added `Math.round()` to three price-parsing functions:\n- `parseEuros()` in `src/money.js` (line 13)\n- `cellCents()` in `src/money.js` (line 25) \n- `decimalCommaToCents()` in `src/locale.js` (line 18)\n\nThis ensures floating-point imprecision is rounded to the nearest cent, so prices like 39.95 are reliably converted to exactly 3995 cents.\n\nWould you like me to commit these changes?",
